>> servings: 4

Heat @olive oil{} in a #large pot{}.
Once hot, add @onion{1}(chopped) and @carrot{2}(sliced) and cook for ~{8%minutes}, until soft.
Season with @salt{}.
Reduce heat to medium, stir in @tomato paste{35%g}, @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), and @rosemary{1%sprig}(finely chopped) and cook ~{2%minutes}, until the tomato paste turns brick red and garlic is aromatic.

Add @chorizo{200%g}(thinly sliced) and sauté until browned, about ~{5%minutes}.
Add @white beans{1%can}. Use a potato masher or fork to roughly mash beans.
This helps them release starch, which will thicken the broth.

Add @chicken stock{4%cups}, @kale{1%bunch}(stemmed and chopped), @white beans{1%can}, @salt{} and @pepper{}.
Gently simmer soup with the lid slightly ajar for ~{20%minutes}.
If you prefer a brothier soup, add 1 cup of water or stock.
Remove lid and stir in @hard cheese{60%g}(grated) and @red wine vinegar{3/2%tsp}.
Serve with extra grated @hard cheese{}.
